============================================================================================================
§4  IS v_msg,λ = 1/ttau LEGITIMATE?  (the Schur τ was not built as v_g+v_R)
============================================================================================================
  (a) The RANK-1 truth.  ρ_g and ρ_R from ONE source share M (⇒ the count cancels in the ratio) and
      move on ONE λ: d log f_g = (1−f_g)dλ, d log f_R = −f_g dλ ⇒ corr = −1 EXACTLY.
         f_g  Var(log k) TRUE    v_g+v_R    ratio   (τ_src=2, n_src=14)
       0.050           0.5000     0.5954     1.19×
       0.250           0.5000     0.4554     0.91×
       0.500           0.5000     0.3929     0.79×
       0.750           0.5000     0.4554     0.91×
       0.950           0.5000     0.5954     1.19×
       0.999           0.5000     0.6419     1.28×
      ⇒ v_g+v_R equals Var(log k) at NO interior f_g.  Its composition part ((1−f)²+f²)/τ understates
        the truth 1/τ by up to 2× (it drops the −1 covariance, worst at f=½), and it DOUBLE-COUNTS
        the shared count (+2/n, which cancels exactly in the ratio k).  On a thin source the +2/n
        over-states it instead.  Neither error is principled: 1/ttau IS the λ variance, use it.

  (b) Does mixing a λ-space gap with the Schur-τ precision break the DL identity?  NO — and here is
      the exact reason: the DELIVERED variance is self-limiting,
            v_deliv = v_msg + max(0, G² − v_msg − v_own) = MAX(v_msg, G² − v_own),
      which is MONOTONE in v_msg and has the v_msg-FREE floor G² − v_own.  So a mis-stated v_msg
      cannot make the message more confident than the observed gap allows.
           G²   v_own |  v_msg=1/ttau   v_deliv |  v_msg=v_g+v_R   v_deliv |  cap 1/(G²−v_own)
       30.800  0.6250 |         0.500   30.1750 |          1.070   30.1750 |            0.0331
        6.600  0.6250 |         0.500    5.9750 |          1.070    5.9750 |            0.1674
        2.000  0.6250 |         0.500    1.3750 |          1.070    1.3750 |            0.7273
        0.500  0.6250 |         0.500    0.5000 |          1.070    1.0700 |       (no excess)
        0.050  0.6250 |         0.500    0.5000 |          1.070    1.0700 |       (no excess)
      ⇒ identical wherever the excess is live (G² > v_msg+v_own).  v_msg only matters where the
        message AGREES with the own belief — precisely where it is harmless.  The only way to break
        the identity is to make the CAP wrong, i.e. to use a gap from a different space: (A-comp)
        caps at 1/(G_c²−v_own,c) = 1/(J̄²·(G_λ²−v_own,λ)) — 1–4× too confident (§1).

  (c) Residual bias of b̂² when the stated v_msg is wrong:  E[b̂²] = b² + (v_msg,true − v_msg,stated).
      v_msg stated=0.500 [    1/ttau (correct)]  b̂²= 30.2554 (b²=30.250)  v_deliv= 30.7554   → precision  0.0325
      v_msg stated=1.070 [      v_g+v_R (n=14)]  b̂²= 29.6695 (b²=30.250)  v_deliv= 30.7395   → precision  0.0325
      v_msg stated=0.050 [10× over-confident τ]  b̂²= 30.7272 (b²=30.250)  v_deliv= 30.7772   → precision  0.0325
      ⇒ the delivered precision is ~invariant to the stated v_msg (the cap), and any UNDER-stated
        v_msg errs toward MORE damping — the §1-safe direction.  Use 1/ttau.

============================================================================================================
§5  THE PIN-SAFETY INVARIANT (the §1 governing principle as an exact inequality).
============================================================================================================
  A message OUT-WEIGHS the own belief iff v_deliv < v_own.  With v_deliv = max(v_msg, G²−v_own):
        message dominates  ⟺  v_msg < v_own  AND  G² < 2·v_own  ⟺  |G| < √2·σ_own.
  (B-λ) applies this in λ — the space the composition DOF lives in — so:
        ▶ NO message can dominate a node's own composition belief unless it agrees with it to
          within √2 own-σ.  A message that disagrees by more can never PIN the node.  That is
          exactly 'pass-0 must be weak and correctable', with no constant.
  (A-comp) applies it in log f_c, where G_c = J̄_c·G_λ and v_own,c = J_c²·v_own,λ, so the same
  crossover lands at  |G_λ| < σ_own,λ·√((1+J_c²)/J̄_c²)  ≥  √2·σ_own,λ  — ALWAYS looser:
       J̄ (mean)  J (own) |  B-λ threshold  A-comp threshold  looser by
           0.500    0.500 |       1.414·σ          2.236·σ      1.58×
           0.500    0.950 |       1.414·σ          2.759·σ      1.95×
           0.557    0.964 |       1.414·σ          2.494·σ      1.76×
           0.270    0.950 |       1.414·σ          5.109·σ      3.61×
           0.900    0.900 |       1.414·σ          1.495·σ      1.06×
           1.000    1.000 |       1.414·σ          1.414·σ      1.00×
  ⇒ (A-comp) lets a message that disagrees with the own belief by up to ~2.5 own-σ still PIN the
    node.  (B-λ) caps it at 1.41 own-σ, for every node, at every f_g.  Over-confidence is the
    one direction the owner forbids ⇒ (B-λ).

  EMPIRICAL CONFIRMATION on the real ψ — the τ stream ALONE (no junction ⇒ cm_*=0), sweeping the
  source composition.  'moved' = (λ_fused − λ_own)/(λ_msg − λ_own): 1 = the message wins, 0 = the
  own belief wins.  The 0.5 crossing is the pinning threshold.
